# __DIST_NAME__

Reference external driver generated by Poly. Replace the sample marker,
inspection metadata, verb, action, and tests with technology-specific behavior.

```shell
uv lock
uv sync --locked --all-groups
uv run poly-driver-test validate
uv run poly-driver-test inspect __PACKAGE_NAME__:driver --workspace tests/fixtures/workspace
uv run poly-driver-test determinism __PACKAGE_NAME__:driver --workspace tests/fixtures/workspace --verb sample-status
uv run ruff format --check .
uv run ruff check .
uv run mypy src tests
uv run pytest
uv build
```

Inspection and planning must remain deterministic and side-effect free. Actions
must cover the requested verb only and declare commands or an execution handler;
they must never cause Poly to infer another verb. The package exposes the same
factory through `poly-driver.toml` and the `poly.drivers` entry-point group.
